{"title":"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> be a continuous function on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f240143a85a508de7721a7548b3b3c545547bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-\\infty, \\infty)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/9/959c6bd6a79e12165e350ecf1a9ec33cd78b7088.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int_{1}^{3} f(x) \\, dx = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"122\" height=\"46\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/2/742680ae93d9e318ce6119a1d6014718f4b0437c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int_{3}^{7} f(x) \\, dx = -3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"136\" height=\"46\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/1/b51b239af548052f9f0bc7ce5c65cf815ba9bfec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int_{5}^{7} f(x) \\, dx = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"122\" height=\"46\" />, what is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fd6e28afc8488e67403d4217a8725b35545b93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int_{1}^{5} f(x) \\, dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"88\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf4d578e749642567f4ce5b76fec6a7b2964570.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 7  \\quad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 10  \\quad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 4  \\quad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2  \\quad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 0  \\quad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"310\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> continuous on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2ef3408d1467035248fea7a912c6f97915eb8c18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a, c]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is in that interval, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/e/63e57b4785028569ba6bd43406d1331f045e3c44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int_{a}^{c} g(x) \\, dx = \\int_{a}^{b} g(x) \\, dx + \\int_{b}^{c} g(x) \\, dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"301\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>This means:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/a/deaf5f4e7dcccc9487bdff1b414f5e1505f4cc60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int_{1}^{7} f(x) \\, dx = \\int_{1}^{3} f(x) \\, dx + \\int_{3}^{7} f(x) \\, dx = 5 - 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"373\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fda1595d50bbb57bf0e0e48232de80ca22e7644.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int_{1}^{7} f(x) \\, dx = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"122\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/c/02c247c9894264d87f4dcf8123ad3e67198ef9af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int_{1}^{7} f(x) \\, dx = \\int_{1}^{5} f(x) \\, dx + \\int_{5}^{7} f(x) \\, dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"308\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68f3b237c7a12f285bb0f8fb1f19b1707a1a3753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 = \\int_{1}^{5} f(x) \\, dx + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"153\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/a/00ac328e85485223db43b6ba35806e7eea7f841d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int_{1}^{5} f(x) \\, dx = 2 - 2 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(E) } 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"231\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2025 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 19 (page does not exist)\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edi